e, using the properties of the expected value, and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X(5X+2)-3] & =\\text{E}[5{X}^{2}+2X-3] \\\\  & =5\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]+2\\text{E}[X]+\\text{E}[-3] \\\\  & =5\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]+2\\text{E}[X]-3 \\\\  & =5(50)+2(-7)-3 \\\\  & =233.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175958 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33fca834-0063-5252-832f-5efb4be6e599" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions Using the Properties of Expected Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b84e972-91af-5283-be7d-7b174d7aa34a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "542" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426760} {:answer/id #uuid "161b6b27-31a6-5f60-9425-0f9c32ebfa5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "590" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426763} {:answer/id #uuid "b3809182-32d0-5d1f-aca6-70df8dd13f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "592" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426773} {:answer/id #uuid "db888a76-ff37-54a2-9ae5-b989f39555be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "594" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426778} {:answer/id #uuid "f53461b4-981e-55c3-801a-8234df8336a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "562" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3809182-32d0-5d1f-aca6-70df8dd13f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "592" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426773} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5a85f0d-532b-5b07-b202-73baf26d36cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86bc7dc6-b40a-53a5-81fd-6b94c073d41e" :question/math-academy-id "q-110008" :question/problem "Compute $\\text{E}[(6Y+4)^{2}]$ if $\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]=12$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=3.$" :question/worked-solution "Expanding out the square inside the expected value, using the properties of the expected value, and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[(6Y+4)^{2}] & =\\text{E}[36{Y}^{2}+48Y+16] \\\\  & =36\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]+48\\text{E}[Y]+\\text{E}[16] \\\\  & =36\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]+48\\text{E}[Y]+16 \\\\  & =36(12)+48(3)+16 \\\\  & =592.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebfe6309-b8a3-5e4c-b2ae-495a91bcc433" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Higher Moments of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b48da996-83e4-5e76-885d-d2f866efdb47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174515} {:answer/id #uuid "beb1e493-b90f-56f2-8837-460b1c3b8a2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174516} {:answer/id #uuid "f94c187e-9eb8-5796-9ed1-fbaddd666f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174517} {:answer/id #uuid "59462356-ec93-5845-9eb3-8534e160e05e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174518} {:answer/id #uuid "6380f064-7b18-5622-943f-749d9634d4bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b48da996-83e4-5e76-885d-d2f866efdb47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174515} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe77e694-ed18-5bfe-9180-33e93463e7c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2d805fb0-bc76-54a9-a263-7551f00436aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-143751" :question/problem "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{10}, & x=0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{4}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{4}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each squared value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{10}+{1}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{2}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{16}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebfe6309-b8a3-5e4c-b2ae-495a91bcc433" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Higher Moments of a Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31869a6a-c7b3-5fd8-aa3e-284f3d59ab95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426764} {:answer/id #uuid "4386d36c-9dbd-5582-8c22-4504cf7121c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426766} {:answer/id #uuid "92d52443-3bd3-516d-bbf6-84b158e700ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426772} {:answer/id #uuid "cce46a42-c639-5945-9a8a-12511515e16d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426776} {:answer/id #uuid "daa8a404-d0e4-57d9-8714-4c89d9ef164f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4386d36c-9dbd-5582-8c22-4504cf7121c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426766} :answer-field/id #uuid "802686da-19e2-5e90-856b-10082948e6d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97f24d3e-df80-5494-a01f-c5ae043371c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-143794" :question/problem "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ |\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}].$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each squared value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{3}\\cdot 0.05+{1}^{3}\\cdot 0.4+{2}^{3}\\cdot 0.1+{3}^{3}\\cdot 0.2+{4}^{3}\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.05+1\\cdot 0.4+8\\cdot 0.1+27\\cdot 0.2+64\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0+0.4+0.8+5.4+16 \\\\  & =22.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175958 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33fca834-0063-5252-832f-5efb4be6e599" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions Using the Properties of Expected Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e36a1d7-0791-58f7-8982-868304ac8df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426761} {:answer/id #uuid "46a8ef29-eaf0-516d-9633-2006fce4fb52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426767} {:answer/id #uuid "6c249428-8d08-51bf-ae81-1bb5765af7ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426769} {:answer/id #uuid "739fc267-7138-5a80-afd7-189d677e4a5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426770} {:answer/id #uuid "c13fd77c-9ad1-5778-b83e-31cad41c6866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c249428-8d08-51bf-ae81-1bb5765af7ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426769} :answer-field/id #uuid "9eed2828-4a7b-5794-87c9-0670f96099bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "07220d09-adbb-5d69-80d7-bbbef5274be7" :question/math-academy-id "q-83949" :question/problem "Compute $\\text{E}[(A+1)(A-3)]$ if $\\text{E}[{A}^{2}]=7$ and $\\text{E}[A]=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Expanding out the square inside the expected value, using the properties of the expected value, and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[(A+1)(A-3)] & =\\text{E}[{A}^{2}-2A-3] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{A}^{2}]+\\text{E}[-2A]+\\text{E}[-3] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{A}^{2}]-2\\text{E}[A]-3 \\\\  & =7-2(2)-3 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
